WEBVTT

00:00:00.267 --> 00:00:03.767
Each customer is now one record,
merged by rules you signed.

00:00:03.767 --> 00:00:05.633
Ask that clean data a question.

00:00:05.633 --> 00:00:08.600
What takes a spreadsheet and a
week should take one sentence,

00:00:08.600 --> 00:00:10.600
and the answer should name its sources.

00:00:10.633 --> 00:00:13.300
In this clip you'll ask in
plain words and share a chat.

00:00:13.300 --> 00:00:15.933
You'll check what search
can find, trace a value,

00:00:15.933 --> 00:00:18.200
and read the memory of
every reply and call.

00:00:18.233 --> 00:00:21.033
Mia asks what was agreed
on the Northwind renewal.

00:00:21.033 --> 00:00:24.100
The answer sits in a March call
and a reply buried in a thread.

00:00:24.100 --> 00:00:26.667
Nobody finds both, and
the quote goes out wrong.

00:00:26.667 --> 00:00:28.300
Every answer needs a source,

00:00:28.300 --> 00:00:31.100
and every reply and call
needs to be remembered once.

00:00:31.167 --> 00:00:33.967
First, ask. In the console: CRM, AI chat.

00:00:33.967 --> 00:00:37.900
Ask about your whole organization,
or one company, contact or deal.

00:00:37.900 --> 00:00:39.367
It reads with your permissions,

00:00:39.367 --> 00:00:42.067
so it never shows what you
couldn't open yourself.

00:00:42.067 --> 00:00:43.800
Your chats are private to you.

00:00:43.800 --> 00:00:46.033
Anything it proposes to change becomes

00:00:46.033 --> 00:00:48.667
an approval request that
a teammate approves,

00:00:48.667 --> 00:00:50.733
never you and never the assistant.

00:00:50.800 --> 00:00:52.533
Or ask your own agent over MCP:

00:00:52.533 --> 00:00:55.167
"What did we agree about
the Northwind renewal,

00:00:55.167 --> 00:00:57.000
and which records is that based on".

00:00:57.000 --> 00:00:59.700
It reads freely and names
where each answer came from.

00:00:59.700 --> 00:01:02.300
Advanced move: always
add that last clause,

00:01:02.300 --> 00:01:04.367
so you can open the sources and check.

00:01:04.400 --> 00:01:07.367
Share creates a read only
link to one conversation,

00:01:07.367 --> 00:01:09.767
handy for showing a colleague
how you got an answer.

00:01:09.767 --> 00:01:13.367
Anyone with the link can read it,
so treat it like a shared document.

00:01:13.367 --> 00:01:15.200
Revoke ends every link for that chat.

00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:19.333
Or ask your agent: "Share my Northwind
chat read only and give me the link".

00:01:19.400 --> 00:01:22.500
Second, search. In the console:
Settings, Search index.

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:25.633
Records are indexed as they
change and swept daily.

00:01:25.633 --> 00:01:30.267
Each object type shows how many records
are indexed, how many have vectors,

00:01:30.267 --> 00:01:33.533
and the embedding model in
use. Reindex now rebuilds it.

00:01:33.533 --> 00:01:37.067
Without an embedding provider,
search still works as plain text,

00:01:37.067 --> 00:01:38.733
but no vectors are stored.

00:01:38.800 --> 00:01:42.833
Or ask your agent: "How much of our
organization can be searched by meaning?

00:01:42.833 --> 00:01:44.867
If vectors are missing, reindex".

00:01:44.867 --> 00:01:48.133
It reads the coverage, queues the
reindex and gives you the job.

00:01:48.133 --> 00:01:51.500
A reindex rebuilds the index
and changes no records.

00:01:51.533 --> 00:01:53.800
Third, lineage, with its honest limit.

00:01:53.800 --> 00:01:56.067
On a company, contact or
deal, open Why this value.

00:01:56.067 --> 00:02:00.067
It shows the source, the rule that
picked it when sources disagreed,

00:02:00.067 --> 00:02:01.800
and the observations behind it.

00:02:01.800 --> 00:02:05.000
For derived values like
a score, and for metrics,

00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:05.933
the trace is partial today.

00:02:05.933 --> 00:02:10.200
It says the value is derived instead
of pretending to a full chain.

00:02:10.233 --> 00:02:14.100
Or ask your agent: "Where did the
employee count on Northwind come from".

00:02:14.100 --> 00:02:16.300
It names the rule and the observations.

00:02:16.300 --> 00:02:18.667
For a derived value it
says what it can show,

00:02:18.667 --> 00:02:21.133
so you never mistake a
summary for a full chain.

00:02:21.167 --> 00:02:24.900
Now the memory. In the
console: CRM, Conversations.

00:02:24.900 --> 00:02:28.100
Every inbound reply is stored
once, whatever the channel.

00:02:28.100 --> 00:02:31.267
It's linked to the person,
company and deal, and labeled.

00:02:31.267 --> 00:02:36.000
The defaults are interested, not now,
objection, referral, wrong person,

00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:39.767
unsubscribe, out of office and
bounce. You can define your own.

00:02:39.767 --> 00:02:43.700
Rules read the reply first, and
a person's label always wins.

00:02:43.767 --> 00:02:46.200
Each label has effects, applied once.

00:02:46.200 --> 00:02:48.033
Every reply stops that
contact's sequences.

00:02:48.033 --> 00:02:52.233
Unsubscribe records the opt out,
and bounce suppresses the address.

00:02:52.233 --> 00:02:54.167
Not now creates a follow
up task in thirty days.

00:02:54.167 --> 00:02:57.633
Objection and referral open
a question for the owner.

00:02:57.633 --> 00:03:00.333
If a model or an agent chose
a label that suppresses,

00:03:00.333 --> 00:03:02.100
the effect waits for a person.

00:03:02.133 --> 00:03:06.300
Or ask your agent: "Show this week's
replies labeled objection or referral,

00:03:06.300 --> 00:03:09.767
and what happened after each". It
reads the labels and the effect log.

00:03:09.767 --> 00:03:12.533
Any next action it proposes
waits for a person.

00:03:12.600 --> 00:03:16.933
Fifth, calls. Transcripts arrive from
a recorder connected through Composio,

00:03:16.933 --> 00:03:20.800
pulled every six hours, or from
a paste, an upload or an agent.

00:03:20.800 --> 00:03:24.900
Each becomes one record on the
timeline, linked to the person, company,

00:03:24.900 --> 00:03:27.900
deal and meeting. It's split
at speaker turns and indexed,

00:03:27.900 --> 00:03:30.867
so search and your agent
can recall what was said.

00:03:30.900 --> 00:03:34.233
Transcripts follow visibility:
organization, team or private.

00:03:34.233 --> 00:03:38.300
A hidden linked record hides them
too. When a person is erased,

00:03:38.300 --> 00:03:39.733
their name is replaced and their

00:03:39.733 --> 00:03:41.833
speaker lines and email
addresses are redacted.

00:03:41.833 --> 00:03:45.733
Lines with no speaker label can't
be attributed, so they stay.

00:03:45.800 --> 00:03:49.033
Or ask your agent: "Add this
call transcript to Northwind,

00:03:49.033 --> 00:03:51.233
then tell me what the
buyer said about price".

00:03:51.233 --> 00:03:53.500
The answer points at
the place in the call.

00:03:53.533 --> 00:03:57.767
Last, coverage. In the console:
CRM, Conversations, Coverage.

00:03:57.767 --> 00:04:00.767
Each source shows whether it's
connected, its records synced,

00:04:00.767 --> 00:04:05.267
and when it last synced. It also shows
the share of your accounts it covers,

00:04:05.267 --> 00:04:07.367
over ninety days by default.

00:04:07.367 --> 00:04:11.400
Or ask your agent: "Which of our
sources cover the fewest accounts".

00:04:11.433 --> 00:04:15.100
The pushback: an assistant that reads
everything will leak, or invent.

00:04:15.100 --> 00:04:18.500
It reads with your permissions, so
it can't show what you can't open.

00:04:18.500 --> 00:04:22.200
Each answer names the records behind
it. The assistant can't write,

00:04:22.200 --> 00:04:24.733
because anything it proposes
waits for a teammate.

00:04:24.733 --> 00:04:27.433
And where it can't trace
a value, it says so.

00:04:27.500 --> 00:04:31.233
The short version: Ask in plain
words, and ask for the sources.

00:04:31.233 --> 00:04:34.100
Search by meaning, and trace a
value as far as the trace goes.

00:04:34.100 --> 00:04:38.567
Replies and calls are stored once and
remembered. Every answer has a source.

00:04:38.633 --> 00:04:41.133
You can ask in plain words, trace a value,

00:04:41.133 --> 00:04:43.233
and trust what your
organization remembers.

00:04:43.233 --> 00:04:46.967
Open AI chat and ask your first
question, with its sources.

00:04:46.967 --> 00:04:51.133
Up next, definitions as code, where
your rules become signed config.
